We see Bill Elliott back in 2016.

02:08:30.000 --> 02:08:30.780
Sixth spot.

02:08:31.530 --> 02:08:34.650
And Jeff Purvis in 32nd, the only car to fall out of the race.

02:08:34.810 --> 02:08:35.990
How about the points?

02:08:36.830 --> 02:08:41.310
Elliott with 35.75, and Davey with 35.05.

02:08:41.710 --> 02:08:42.630
That's a 60...

02:08:42.630 --> 02:08:43.530
That's an 8, Bob.

02:08:43.810 --> 02:08:45.510
Or 35.08, right.

02:08:45.670 --> 02:08:46.970
67-point difference.

02:08:47.570 --> 02:08:48.650
Kowicki remains third.

02:08:48.650 --> 02:08:49.810
You'll have to subtract that.

02:08:49.930 --> 02:08:50.870
144 points.

02:08:50.930 --> 02:08:52.690
Okay, and here are the second ten.

02:08:52.890 --> 02:08:55.980
Petty, Rudd, Waltrip, Wallace, and Levante.

02:08:56.790 --> 02:08:59.750
Notice that in 11th through 15th now,

02:08:59.750 --> 02:08:59.910
that

02:09:00.480 --> 02:09:02.940
Dale Earnhardt has dropped two more positions.

02:09:02.940 --> 02:09:05.080
He came into this event 12th in the points.

02:09:05.100 --> 02:09:07.030
He drops to 14th.

02:09:07.150 --> 02:09:10.330
Marlon is 15th and then 16 through 20 in the points.

02:09:10.960 --> 02:09:14.680
Jeff Bodine, Ken Schrader, Ted Musgrave, Dale Jarrett,

02:09:15.260 --> 02:09:19.060
and Dick Trickle 20th in the Quest for the Cup championship.

02:09:19.580 --> 02:09:22.960
The two drivers that are continuing to battle it out for the championship

02:09:22.960 --> 02:09:25.220
are next to each other back in the garage area,

02:09:25.380 --> 02:09:27.770
Davey Allison and Bill Elliott.

02:09:28.010 --> 02:09:29.510
We'll be back to wrap it up in a moment.

02:09:32.080 --> 02:09:35.560
Once again, a review of the top five finishers here in North Wilkesboro.

02:09:35.760 --> 02:09:41.610
Jeff Bodine, the winner, Mark Martin, second, then Kyle Petty, Rusty Wallace, and Sterling Marlin.

02:09:42.190 --> 02:09:47.210
Our next telecast of a Winston Cup event will come on Sunday, November 15th,

02:09:47.250 --> 02:09:49.570
the Hooters 500 from Atlanta Motor Speedway.

02:09:49.790 --> 02:09:53.090
It'll be our final telecast of the year, the final race of the year.

02:09:53.230 --> 02:09:56.630
We'll crown the champion and we'll say goodbye to King Richard Petty.

02:09:56.980 --> 02:09:59.970
And then following the race, we will have the...

02:10:00.000 --> 02:10:03.240
The Portrait of a King, and our salute to Richard Petty

02:10:03.240 --> 02:10:05.240
that Sunday, November the 15th,

02:10:05.590 --> 02:10:08.690
immediately following our coverage of the Hooters 500

02:10:08.690 --> 02:10:10.470
from Atlanta Motor Speedway.

02:10:11.050 --> 02:10:14.510
Domination here at North Wilkesboro today by Jeff Bodine

02:10:14.510 --> 02:10:16.630
as he picks up his second consecutive win

02:10:16.630 --> 02:10:18.850
in NASCAR Winston Cup competition.

02:10:19.340 --> 02:10:23.280
Thanks to Ned Jarrett, Benny Parsons, John Kernan, and Dr. Jerry Punch.

02:10:23.420 --> 02:10:25.100
Thanks for joining us on this Monday.

02:10:25.460 --> 02:10:27.060
For now, this is Bob Jenkins.

02:10:27.550 --> 02:10:28.510
So long, everyone.
